Register the target once in the shell constructor:

```csharp
Routing.RegisterRoute("productdetails", typeof(ProductDetailsPage));
```

Pass a scalar ID in the URI and await navigation:

```csharp
string id = Uri.EscapeDataString(selectedProduct.Id);
await Shell.Current.GoToAsync($"productdetails?id={id}");
```

Pass the object without serializing it by using the parameter overload:

```csharp
var parameters = new ShellNavigationQueryParameters
{
    ["product"] = selectedProduct
};
await Shell.Current.GoToAsync("productdetails", parameters);
```

Keep both receiving paths in the view model:

```csharp
public sealed class ProductDetailsViewModel : IQueryAttributable
{
    public string? ProductId { get; private set; }
    public Product? Product { get; private set; }

    public void ApplyQueryAttributes(IDictionary<string, object> query)
    {
        if (query.TryGetValue("id", out var id))
            ProductId = id?.ToString();

        if (query.TryGetValue("product", out var product) &&
            product is Product selected)
            Product = selected;
    }
}
```

Shell applies query attributes after the page has assigned this view model as its binding context.
